{"id": 33, "ts": 1779479468.1642427, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "agent_1", "message": "Based on the combined evidence, Candidate\u202fC stands out for the core safety\u2011critical criteria: 100\u202f% reliability (my interview), strong stress resilience and technical competence (Agent\u202f2\u2019s notes), rapid and correct decision\u2011making (shared dossier), and a positive crew atmosphere (my interview). The main concerns are communication difficulty, an egocentric style, and a lack of willingness to pursue further education, which could affect crew cooperation and adaptability. Compared with the alternatives, Candidate\u202fB, while technically capable and stress\u2011resilient, has been noted as grumpy and uncooperative; Candidate\u202fA shows strong situational awareness but struggles with organization and accepting criticism; Candidate\u202fD demonstrates problem\u2011solving and responsibility but we lack any concrete data on crew cooperation or professional communication, and the interview notes flag arrogance and weak leadership. Given the weight of the safety\u2011relevant criteria, I recommend moving forward with Candidate\u202fC, while planning targeted development on communication and continuous learning.\nMETADATA_JSON:\n{\"agent\": \"agent_1\", \"vote\": \"Candidate C\"}"}
